  "declared_proposition": "For a positive accelerated Collatz cycle with cyclic valuation word 1^k 2^m, put Delta=2^(k+2m)-3^(k+m)>0. In addition to the TICKET-215 near-collision bound, integer closure forces the exact necessary identity Delta=gcd(3^k-2^k,4^m-3^m). At the unique first-positive candidate m for each 1<=k<=4096, exact integer arithmetic finds no gcd equality.",
  "mathematical_argument": "TICKET-215 proves that a cycle forces Delta to divide C=3^k-2^k. Write E=4^m-3^m. The exact identity Delta=2^k E-3^m C shows that gcd(C,E) divides Delta. Conversely Delta divides C, and the same identity gives Delta|2^k E. Since Delta is odd, Delta|E. Thus Delta divides gcd(C,E), proving equality. The audit recomputes the first positive crossing and the gcd with arbitrary-precision integers.",
